          "end": 142.71,
          "en": "which is called a native query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 142.71,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "But what if you don't want to use SQL?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "In that case, you can use something called HQL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "which is Hibernate Query Language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 149.947,
          "en": "And now you're thinking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 149.947,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "\"Oh, we have to learn a new language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "Not exactly. If you know the basics of SQL, we are good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "It's because HQL is derived from SQL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 160.35,
          "en": "What is different?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 163.62,
          "en": "In SQL, you work with databases, you work with tables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 163.62,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "you work with the columns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.32,
          "en": "In the HQL, you fire almost the same query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 169.32,
          "end": 173.13,
          "en": "The difference is instead of using the name of a table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 173.13,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "you use the name of the entity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 177.42000000000002,
          "en": "Instead of using the name of a column, you use the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 181.14,
          "en": "of a property, and that's what HQL is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 181.14,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "It also makes certain things easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "Example, let's say if you want to fetch everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 189.6,
          "en": "from a table, normally we say SELECT * FROM the table name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 191.61,
          "en": "let's say table student.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "But in case of HQL, you don't have to say SELECT *.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 197.34,
          "en": "I mean, why do you have to mention SELECT *",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "when you're seeing star there?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 198.93,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "In HQL, you simply say FROM student.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "I mean, this student is not a table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 205.77,
          "en": "it's a entity, and that's how you do it, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 210.243,
